            <ArticleTitle>A protocol for investigating the association of vaccination and anti-NMDA receptor encephalitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-237</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anti-N-methyl-D-aspartate (Anti-NMDA) receptor encephalitis is an acute autoimmune neurological disorder that can be triggered by virus, H1N1/tetanus/diphtheria/pertussis and polio vaccines or by presence of a tumor. The association between anti-NMDA receptor encephalitis and Japanese encephalitis vaccination was examined and a general protocol of phylogenetic method which details the steps and code and an example of its utility is provided. The approach used here is potentially useful for analyzing the relationship between vaccines and diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
